  "checks": [
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.indexed_cone_paper: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:992-1008 assumes 'HomogCovariance', 'Γ ≠ 0', supplied 'GroundFamily F' and '0 < ϱ', 'ϱ < 1 / 2'; TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:4-10 supplies the physical ground family under nonzero H:homog, and :229 assumes '0 < varrho < 1/2'. The documented abstraction is legitimate: every GroundFamily property follows from C16. The existential order, integer B, product order, positivity and cStar=aStar*jStar/4 match :229-245,326-327. Ledger:1109 and claims.yaml:2003 are faithful."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.indexed_cone: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:963-975 assumes 'G : GroundFamily F', '0 < ϱ', 'ϱ < 1 / 2'; TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:229-242 assumes the C16 family and the same strict rho range. Both choose B, omega, epsilon and c before every N, chain and D. Pointwise closeness is equivalent to the displayed max/sup bound here. Ledger:1110 and claims.yaml:2010 match, including the exact constant established at :326-327."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.paramI: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:74 defines 'paramI := Icc 0 1', without hypotheses; TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:4 says 'Let I = [0,1]' in unlabelled setup. Ledger:1111 and claims.yaml:2017 match; no separate labelled theorem is claimed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.isCompact_paramI: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:77 proves 'IsCompact paramI', without additional hypotheses; TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:4 fixes '[0,1]'. This is a valid Lean auxiliary rather than a separately labelled manuscript assertion. Ledger:1112 and claims.yaml:2024 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily: P:compact-F-projection",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:83-126 supplies bounded linear P and ell, data e0 and bounded obs, positive rates/gap, eigenrelations for 'σ ∈ paramI', '0 ≤ t', continuity and positive infima. TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:48-52,270-286,339-348 provides those properties under its compact-family/common-trial hypotheses at :4-10; raw-block setup :16-17 supplies e0 and bounded O_phi. No field is stronger than these outputs. Ledger:1061-1085,1113 and claims.yaml:2031 accurately describe the supplied interface."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.Pi: E:compact-F-projection",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:133 defines 'Pi σ := (G.ell σ).smulRight (G.e σ)'; TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:270-273 defines 'Pi_sigma=e_sigma ell_sigma'. Ledger:1114 and claims.yaml:2038 agree. Projection properties concern σ in I; arbitrary extensions outside I do not enter the result."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.Q: E:compact-F-projection",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:136 defines 'Q σ := id - G.Pi σ'; TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:272-273 defines 'Q_sigma=I-Pi_sigma'. Ledger:1115 and claims.yaml:2045 faithfully state this definition."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.aStar: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:139 defines 'aStar := iInf σ : paramI, G.ell σ G.e0'; TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:254 defines 'a_*=inf_I ell_s(e_0)'. Ledger:1116 and claims.yaml:2052 match. Compact continuity ensures the real infimum has its intended bounded-set meaning."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.jStar: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:142 defines 'jStar := iInf σ : paramI, G.obs (G.e σ)'; TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:254 defines 'j_*=inf_I O_phi(e_s)'. Ledger:1117 and claims.yaml:2059 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.Pi_apply: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:145 states, for arbitrary σ and x, 'G.Pi σ x = G.ell σ x • G.e σ'; TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:272 gives 'Pi_sigma=e_sigma ell_sigma' on I. Ledger:1118 and claims.yaml:2066 correctly present the defining application identity as a Lean auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.Q_apply: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:148 states 'G.Q σ x = x - G.ell σ x • G.e σ', without membership assumptions; TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:272 defines 'Q_sigma=I-Pi_sigma'. Ledger:1119 and claims.yaml:2073 faithfully describe the auxiliary unfolding."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.ell_P: E:compact-F-eigen",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:151-154 assumes 'σ ∈ paramI', '0 ≤ t' and concludes 'ell σ (P σ t x)=exp(lam σ*t)*ell σ x'. TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:277-280 has 'Pi_sigma P_sigma(t)=exp(lambda_sigma t)Pi_sigma', with ell(e)=1, and :325 states the dual identity explicitly. Ledger:1120 and claims.yaml:2080 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.P_e: E:compact-F-eigen",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:157-160 assumes 'σ ∈ paramI', '0 ≤ t' and proves 'P σ t (e σ)=exp(lam σ*t) • e σ'. TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:277-280 gives the growing projection identity, and :326 explicitly gives the vector identity. Ledger:1121 and claims.yaml:2087 are faithful."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.ell_Q: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:163 assumes 'σ ∈ paramI' and proves 'ell σ (Q σ x)=0'. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:280-281 uses 'ell_s(r)=0' and 'r=Q_s z', with normalization supplied by compact-family TeX:278. Ledger:1122 and claims.yaml:2094 match this algebraic cone identity."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.Q_Q: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:167 assumes 'σ ∈ paramI' and proves 'Q σ (Q σ x)=Q σ x'. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:280-281 identifies the kernel residual with Q_s z; compact-family TeX:272,278 supplies the complementary projection and normalization. Idempotence is the same implicit projection algebra, not a different proof route. Ledger:1123 and claims.yaml:2101 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.decomp: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:171 proves 'x=ell σ x • e σ+Q σ x' for arbitrary σ,x; TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:280-281 writes 'z=Ae_s+r', 'A=ell_s(z)', 'r=Q_s z'. The identity itself needs no cone positivity. Ledger:1124 and claims.yaml:2108 faithfully state that algebraic component."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.P_Q: E:compact-F-eigen",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:175-178 assumes 'σ ∈ paramI', '0 ≤ t' and concludes 'P σ t (Q σ x)=Q σ (P σ t x)'. TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:279 says 'P_sigma(t)Pi_sigma=Pi_sigma P_sigma(t)'; with Q=I-Pi at :272 this is precisely the stated consequence. Ledger:1125 and claims.yaml:2115 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.norm_Q_le: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:181 states '‖G.Q σ‖ ≤ 1 + ‖G.Pi σ‖', without membership assumptions; TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:258 introduces 'M_Q=1+M_P' after bounding Pi. This is its underlying triangle bound. Ledger:1126 and claims.yaml:2122 are accurate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.norm_Pi: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:185 states '‖Pi σ‖=‖ell σ‖*‖e σ‖' for arbitrary σ; TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:272 defines the rank-one operator, but does not separately assert this exact norm formula. Ledger:1127 and claims.yaml:2129 correctly identify an auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.norm_Pi_sub_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:190-191 gives the displayed two-term bound for arbitrary b,c. TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:328-329 invokes 'bounded bilinear multiplication' to obtain continuity, without this explicit inequality. Ledger:1128 and claims.yaml:2136 accurately state the Lean-only estimate and its role."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.exp_ge_one: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:209-211 assumes 'σ ∈ paramI', '0 ≤ t' and concludes '1 ≤ exp(lam σ*t)'. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:297 uses 'Since lambda_c > 0' for exactly this normalization estimate. Ledger:1129 and claims.yaml:2143 agree; the conservative auxiliary designation makes no separate labelled-result claim."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.chainState: E:raw-block-positive-product",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:219-221 defines the recurrence '0 => e0', 'm+1 => D m B (chainState ... m)', without flow assumptions. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:239 has 'D_N(u)D_(N-1)(B)...D_0(B)e_0'. Ledger:1130 and claims.yaml:2150 correctly identify the state before the terminal factor."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.chainState_zero: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:224-225 states 'chainState D B e0 0=e0', without extra hypotheses. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:239 supplies the ordered product convention, not a separately labelled recurrence. Ledger:1131 and claims.yaml:2157 match the auxiliary unfolding."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.chainState_succ: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:228-229 states 'chainState ... (m+1)=D m B (chainState ... m)' for arbitrary m. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:239 uses the same left multiplication order. Ledger:1132 and claims.yaml:2164 correctly describe an unfolding auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PARTIAL",
      "reason": "W2: IndexedCone.lean:251-284 permits arbitrary positive lower margins 'a_le', 'j_le', 'Cg_nonneg : 0 ≤ Cg', 'ηg_nonneg : 0 ≤ ηg' and 'ν_nonneg : 0 ≤ ν'. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:249-266 fixes the actual infima, 'C_gap ≥ 1', 'eta_gap > 0', 'nu > 0' and specific max bounds. Ledger:1133 and :1092 say 'exactly the TeX inequalities'; that is not the type. claims.yaml:2171 also needs to distinguish sufficient relaxed conditions from the exact choices."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.norm_Q_le: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:291 assumes 'K : ConeConstants G ϱ', 'σ ∈ paramI' and proves '‖Q σ‖ ≤ 1+K.MP'. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:258 sets 'M_Q=1+M_P' with M_P bounding Pi. Ledger:1134 and claims.yaml:2178 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.norm_PQ_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:296-298 assumes K, 'σ ∈ paramI', '0 ≤ t' and bounds '‖P σ t (Q σ y)‖' by exp(lam*t)*Cg*exp(-ηg*t)*‖y‖. TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:344-348 supplies the normalized operator estimate. Ledger:1135 and claims.yaml:2185 accurately describe its vector application as an auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.step_ell: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:315-317 assumes K, 'c ∈ paramI', '0 ≤ t', '‖D-P c t‖ ≤ K.ε', and arbitrary z; TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:283,295-300 uses the same operator perturbation and dual-norm bound for entrance/full blocks. Ledger:1136 and claims.yaml:2192 faithfully give the pointwise amplitude estimate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.step_Q: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:333-336 assumes K, 'c ∈ paramI', '0 ≤ t', '‖D-P c t‖ ≤ K.ε' and gives the residual bound with q=Cg*exp(-ηg*t). TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:284,304-306 uses this bound with q_B. Ledger:1137 and claims.yaml:2199 match; the q factor is the time-dependent complementary decay."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.step_obs: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:352-356 assumes K, 'c ∈ paramI', '0 ≤ t', operator closeness and arbitrary z, and bounds O(Dz) by its growing contribution minus complementary and perturbation errors. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:315-323 uses the same decomposition and errors. Ledger:1138 is a shortened accurate description; claims.yaml:2206 gives the matching formula."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.rebase: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:390-394 assumes adjacent 'b,c ∈ paramI', '0 ≤ ell_b(z)' and the cone residual bound; TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:280-293 assumes an old-cone state and the same adjacency, giving norm, amplitude and residual estimates. The additional zero-amplitude boundary is trivial because it forces z=0. Ledger:1139 is accurate as a shortened cone statement; claims.yaml:2213 states the exact non-strict hypothesis."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.qB_nonneg: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:424-425 derives '0 ≤ K.Cg*exp(-(K.ηg*K.B))' from K.Cg_nonneg. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:249-264 has 'C_gap ≥ 1' and defines q_B by this exponential. Ledger:1140 and claims.yaml:2220 correctly state a nonnegativity auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.entrance: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "reason": "W1: IndexedCone.lean:430-433 assumes arbitrary K and closeness and concludes 'exp(lam_b*B)*(K.a/2) ≤ ell_b(D e0)'; it does not assume 'K.a=G.aStar'. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:286 gives 'exp(lambda_b B)a_*/2'. Ledger:1141 substitutes a_* for K.a and therefore overstates this declaration. claims.yaml:2227 correctly uses a."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.block: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:478-482 assumes K, 'ϱ < 1/2', adjacent indices, positive old amplitude, cone residual and full-block closeness. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:288-313 has the same cone/adjoining-block conditions and multiplier 'exp(lambda_c B)(1-varrho)'. Ledger:1142 and claims.yaml:2234 agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.terminal: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "reason": "W1: IndexedCone.lean:559-562 assumes arbitrary K, adjacency, a closed-cone state, '0 ≤ u' and closeness, and concludes 'exp(lam_c*u)*(K.j/2*ell_b(z)) ≤ obs(Dz)'. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:315-325 obtains the j_*/2 terminal factor. Ledger:1143 writes j_* although K.j need not equal G.jStar. claims.yaml:2241 correctly uses j. The canonical equality is supplied only by exists_coneConstants."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.chain_cone: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:617-626 assumes K, 'ϱ < 1/2', chain membership/adjacency and closeness through N; for 'm+1 ≤ N' it proves the amplitude lower bound, strict positivity and cone residual bound. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:282-313,325-327 performs precisely entrance plus the intermediate-block induction. Ledger:1144 and claims.yaml:2248 match, using the abstract margin a."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.ConeConstants.positive_product_of_constants: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:679-688 assumes K, 'ϱ < 1/2', '1 ≤ N', chain conditions, closeness and 'u ∈ [0,B]', and proves the product bound and positive lower expression with 'K.a*K.j/4'. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:229-242,325-327 gives the canonical specialization. Ledger:1145 explicitly uses a*j/4, and claims.yaml:2255 matches. W2 concerns the description of K, not this deduction."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.ell_e0_continuousOn: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:723-724 derives 'ContinuousOn (fun σ => G.ell σ G.e0) paramI' from G.ell_cont. TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:275-276 gives norm continuity of the duals, and :329-332 uses continuity of their evaluation on e0. Ledger:1146 and claims.yaml:2262 correctly present the auxiliary continuity result."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.obs_e_continuousOn: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:727-728 derives 'ContinuousOn (fun σ => G.obs (G.e σ)) paramI' from G.e_cont and bounded obs. TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:275-276,330-332 asserts the corresponding continuity used for positive margins. Ledger:1147 and claims.yaml:2269 match the auxiliary statement."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.aStar_le: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS_WITH_NOTES",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:732-735 assumes 'σ ∈ paramI' and concludes 'G.aStar ≤ G.ell σ G.e0'; TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:254 defines a_* as the infimum. Ledger:1148 is faithful. claims.yaml:2276 additionally says the infimum is 'attained'; this is mathematically true from compact continuity but is not this declaration's conclusion. See W7."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.jStar_le: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:738-741 assumes 'σ ∈ paramI' and concludes 'G.jStar ≤ G.obs (G.e σ)'. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:254 defines j_* as the corresponding infimum. Ledger:1149 and claims.yaml:2283 match; boundedness below is derived from compact continuity."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.GroundFamily.Pi_bounded_continuous: P:compact-F-projection",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:745-779 assumes G and proves '(∃ M, ∀ σ ∈ paramI, ‖Pi σ‖ ≤ M) ∧ ContinuousOn Pi paramI' from e_cont and ell_cont. TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:275-276 states norm continuity and uniform boundedness of the rank-one projections. Ledger:1150 and claims.yaml:2290 match this projection clause, without claiming the entire proposition is proved."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.exists_coneConstants: L:raw-block-indexed-cone",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:788-789 assumes G and '0 < ϱ', concluding existence of K with 'K.a=G.aStar' and 'K.j=G.jStar'. Its proof :795-953 chooses gap bounds, aperture, integer B, nu, omega and epsilon in the TeX order. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:249-277 makes those choices under positive rho; the extra rho upper bound is not needed for existence. Ledger:1151 and claims.yaml:2297 are accurate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.scalarFamily: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:1016-1040 constructs 'GroundFamily ℝ' with P=exp(t)id, e=1, ell=id, lam=1, e0=1, obs=id and d0=1, without supplied hypotheses. TeX integrated_compact_mean_family.tex:4-19 concerns physical potential families and contains no such scalar example. Ledger:1152 and claims.yaml:2304 correctly label it a Lean non-vacuity auxiliary, not a manuscript result."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.scalarFamily_aStar: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:1043-1045 states 'scalarFamily.aStar=1', without extra hypotheses. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:254 defines the general margin but contains no scalar specialization. Ledger:1153 and claims.yaml:2311 faithfully describe this Lean-only auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.IndexedCone.scalarFamily_jStar: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "IndexedCone.lean:1048-1050 states 'scalarFamily.jStar=1', without extra hypotheses. TeX integrated_raw_block_lower.tex:254 defines the general observable margin but contains no scalar example. Ledger:1154 and claims.yaml:2318 match the auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "PARA-IndexedCone",
      "verdict": "PARTIAL",
      "reason": "The headline result, supplied C16 interface, arbitrary real normed space, generalized e0 norm, carried-unused covariance assumptions, undocumented formal link to Gamma and exact final constant are accurately disclosed at statement-ledger.md:1048-1105. GroundFamily adds no stronger C16 property. However, :1092 calls ConeConstants 'exactly the TeX's inequalities' without disclosing its arbitrary lower margins and relaxed sign/bound requirements; see W2. The data/observable source line citation is also slightly wrong; see W5."
    },
    {
